    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the high-upside pairing of **Yordan Alvarez** (79.78) and **Junior Caminero** (76.37). **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Ginn, where his elite 0.460 xwOBA and the #2 lineup spot make him our primary engine for counting stats. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** earns the highest park-adjusted boost of the day (+16%), signaling a prime breakout opportunity against Rogers. In our pursuit of stolen bases\u2014the league's scarcest category\u2014**Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.51) remains a mandatory start. His promotion to the leadoff spot combined with a 14% dynamic platoon edge against Hancock makes him our most efficient speed-threat play, providing the necessary leverage to maintain our standing in the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the benching of **Jacob Gonzalez** (37.99) and **Gary Sanchez** (37.56), both of whom fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Jacob Gonzalez** was hindered primarily by a challenging matchup against Yamamoto and a bottom-third order placement that stifled his scoring potential. Similarly, despite the power profile of **Gary Sanchez**, he was relegated to the pine due to an ugly BvP history against Sale (35 PA) and a significant SP skill penalty. As we navigate a day with no major weather flags, we are prioritizing the superior matchup efficiency of **Dillon Dingler** (57.10) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.33) over these fringe bench options to protect our game caps while maximizing daily output. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, who remain sidelined and unavailable to contribute to today\u2019s lineup. We will rely on our utility depth, specifically **Chase Meidroth** (53.18), to fill the gaps. While **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.03) and **Pedro Ramirez** (40.59) are clearing our minimum floor, their starts are tenuous; they are leveraged on volume rather than matchup dominance. We continue to hold **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Josh Smith**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Luis Pena** in reserve, prepared to rotate them into the lineup should volatility strike our primary starters during the afternoon sessions.",
